The runner applies only a setup timeout, not a per-MLP FLOP budget during setup. Since the Sobol normal lattice is independent of the weights, I’m going to cache the seed-0 lattice in `setup` and use it only when `mlp.seed == 0`; other seeds fall back to the normal predict-time generation. This keeps predictions seeded from `mlp.seed` while amortizing shared input construction when the suite uses seed 0.
